{"title":"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Carl decided to fence in his rectangular garden. He bought <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> fence posts, placed one on each of the four corners, and spaced out the rest evenly along the edges of the garden, leaving exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> yards between neighboring posts. The longer side of his garden, including the corners, has twice as many posts as the shorter side, including the corners. What is the area, in square yards, of Carl's garden?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/d/78da4658b9b0ec6afea24e98da4874676555ef58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 256\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 336\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 384\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 448\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 512$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"439\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To start, use algebra to determine the number of posts on each side. You have (the long sides count for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because there are twice as many) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/b/b5ba487f83127c2da86fd4e407274e3fbe7404d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6x = 20 + 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"93\" height=\"14\" /> (each corner is double counted so you must add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />) Making the shorter end have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and the longer end have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/0/020d49e2e3bdb985b9c0cc661ec76736f35b0068.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$((8-1) \\cdot 4) \\cdot ((4-1) \\cdot 4) = 28 \\cdot 12 = 336$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"322\" height=\"20\" />. Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/8/d38341fe98e716a4e143ed51dcfbc01efa659a9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 336}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"73\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>~Albert471\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To start, allocate 4 posts from the total 20 to be the corners. Now 16 posts are left. Pairing each long and short side together, you have 8 posts for a segment of long and short (For rectangle ABCD, AB = CD, AC = BD, we are taking what is originally AB + BC + CD + DA = 16, and making it AB + AC = 8). From 8, you need two numbers that add up too 8, that when you add 2 to both of them are at a 1:2 ratio. Brute force says these numbers are 6 and 2. 6 + 2 = 12, and (6+2) = 2(2+2). Then it is trivial to calculate area, as the long side has 8 posts, short side has 4, the total length of the long side is 28, and the short side 12. 28 x 12 = 336.\n</p><p>~Shadow-18\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/2/e9234aa42c2e299b20cfdc790b85b6a29c5b0394.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(0.8cm); import graph;  // Shift amounts real shift = 18bp / 0.8cm;  // Points on perimeter for (int x = 1; x &lt;= 8; ++x) {     dot((x, 1));     dot((x, 4)); } for (int y = 2; y &lt;= 3; ++y) {     dot((1, y));     dot((8, y)); }  // Draw rectangle draw((1,1) -- (8,1) -- (8,4) -- (1,4) -- cycle, linewidth(0.8bp));  // Label left side, m draw(brace((0.7,1), (0.7,4), amplitude=10bp/0.8cm), linewidth(0.8bp)); label(&quot;$m$&quot;, (0.7, 2.5) + (-shift, 0));  // Label top side, n draw(brace((1,4.3), (8,4.3), amplitude=10bp/0.8cm), linewidth(0.8bp)); label(&quot;$n$&quot;, (4.5, 4.3) + (0, shift)); [/asy]\" width=\"322\" height=\"165\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of fenceposts on the shorter side, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of fenceposts on the longer side. We are given that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/9/3c9f4ff271bbb580014772ffdd884bb601c6e778.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n = 2m.\\]\" width=\"63\" height=\"12\" />\nSince there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> fenceposts in total, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/f/b9fd67b52f3056899c4aa5f1c3dcbe48c339172c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2(m+n) - 4 = 20\\]\" width=\"145\" height=\"18\" />\nbecause the corners are counted twice. Solving the system of equations, we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/0/500fb9788ed8553a319dd49cb6262faebcacc88b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/4/1d4f171162b090bab7ce5dfa1c58715850530ba5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=8$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />. Because the fenceposts are spaced <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> yards apart and the number of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-yard spaces is one less than the number of fenceposts (see the fencepost error/off-by-one error), the area of the garden is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/3/ef348fb302bc6d32761f8e2287004b72c6e1c7e3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(4(m-1)) \\cdot (4(n-1)) = 4\\cdot 3 \\cdot 4 \\cdot 7 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 336}\\]\" width=\"373\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>~Blosp\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B\">2016 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a hre